This code validates a planGroupCode against configured Cosmos group codes using the format:

PREFIX:CODE:DATE

Functionality:
1. Parse the incoming planGroupCode into prefix, code, and date.
2. If the prefix belongs to a known mismatched/excluded group, return false.
   Example: CAL, MSP, MEC, FLA, PPL, MTK -> false.
3. If the prefix is not one of the special Cosmos comparison prefixes
   (NTL, OEB, BNA, OHO), return true.
4. For the special prefixes, compare the plan code/date against the configured
   Cosmos code/date values having the same prefix.
5. BNA/OHO -> return true only when CODE and DATE match.
6. NTL/OEB -> return true only when CODE and DATE do NOT match.

Examples:
Cosmos config: BNA:90330:20220303
Plan:          BNA:90330:20220303 -> true
Plan:          BNA:99999:20220303 -> false

Cosmos config: NTL:90110:20220101
Plan:          NTL:90110:20220101 -> false
Plan:          NTL:99999:20220101 -> true

Plan:          CAL:12345:20220101 -> false
Plan:          XYZ:12345:20220101 -> true


/**
 * Validates the supplied plan group code against the configured Cosmos group codes.
 *
 * <p>The expected group-code format is {@code PREFIX:CODE:DATE}.</p>
 *
 * <p>Business rules:</p>
 * <ul>
 *     <li>Returns {@code false} for prefixes configured as mismatched/excluded.</li>
 *     <li>Returns {@code true} for valid prefixes that do not require special
 *         Cosmos code/date comparison.</li>
 *     <li>For BNA and OHO, returns {@code true} only when the CODE and DATE
 *         match a configured Cosmos value with the same prefix.</li>
 *     <li>For NTL and OEB, returns {@code true} only when the CODE and DATE
 *         do not match any configured Cosmos value with the same prefix.</li>
 *     <li>Returns {@code false} when the input is null, blank, or invalid.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * @param planGroupCode plan group code in {@code PREFIX:CODE:DATE} format
 * @return {@code true} when the plan group code satisfies the applicable
 *         prefix-specific business rule; otherwise {@code false}
 */
